WEBVTT

00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:08.342
The Irresponsible Captain
Tylor

00:00:09.111 --> 00:00:11.981
We may be off the maps...
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:11.981 --> 00:00:14.040
...but let's stay on this voyage.
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:14.884 --> 00:00:19.014
I will be holding, never let you go.

00:00:20.589 --> 00:00:23.426
Whatever we may want...
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:23.426 --> 00:00:25.553
...we'll take as we need.
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:26.329 --> 00:00:30.356
So let's just go wherever we please!
Omoi no Mama Yukou!

00:00:32.068 --> 00:00:34.837
Make me your partner...
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:34.837 --> 00:00:37.465
...on this journey.
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:41.335
One that you trust more than words!
Michizure ni Shite

00:00:42.778 --> 00:00:47.442
Come on now and sail away for future!
Imasugu sail away for future

00:00:48.451 --> 00:00:49.952
Things are waiting...
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:49.952 --> 00:00:53.149
...that we've never seen before!
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:54.991 --> 00:00:57.159
Just take your cares...
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:00:57.159 --> 00:01:01.220
...and throw them all away.
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:01:01.464 --> 00:01:06.094
Come together, just think of tomorrow.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:09.360
Let's go!

00:01:12.842 --> 00:01:15.970
THE TAIL OF THE LIZARD'S TAIL

00:01:28.057 --> 00:01:30.457
As you can see, this
circuit chip will access...

00:01:30.526 --> 00:01:33.086
...the standard model
KI-302 radio transmitter...

00:01:33.162 --> 00:01:36.791
...which is installed
in all UPSF destroyers...

00:01:36.866 --> 00:01:39.300
...and create a radio wave
field around the ship.

00:01:40.169 --> 00:01:43.969
If you used this, any Raalgon
forces using interstellar radar...

00:01:44.173 --> 00:01:46.942
...would see one
ship as a large fleet.

00:01:46.942 --> 00:01:47.738
Excellent.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.506
But what do you want
a chip like this for?

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.805
Tell no one else of this!

00:01:53.082 --> 00:01:53.741
Yes, sir!

00:02:26.916 --> 00:02:29.077
Whoa, what's that
big thing out there?

00:02:29.585 --> 00:02:31.610
Gotta hand it to the UPSF.

00:02:31.921 --> 00:02:34.719
Building something that
big is really impressive!

00:02:35.191 --> 00:02:37.318
Mr. Yamamoto, what is it?

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.425
Never mind that, Captain.

00:02:39.695 --> 00:02:42.129
You're going to be meeting
with the commanders soon.

00:02:42.465 --> 00:02:43.599
You don't want to
make a bad impression.

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:45.430
Well, I don't know!

00:02:45.668 --> 00:02:48.762
Oh? What can it be?

00:02:49.171 --> 00:02:50.604
Maybe it's a survey ship.

00:02:50.873 --> 00:02:53.706
Or a military
recreation station!

00:02:53.909 --> 00:02:56.078
With movie theaters,
pools, restaurants...

00:02:56.078 --> 00:02:58.672
...and maybe even
an aesthetic salon!

00:02:59.181 --> 00:03:01.115
I wonder if they give
discounts to captains?

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.048
Captain! This is hardly the
way to act while on duty!

00:03:04.286 --> 00:03:07.119
Oh, I'm sure lieutenant commanders
get a discount too, Yuriko.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.520
Lieutenant Yamamoto,
won't you say something to him?!

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.928
Just have to wait
a little longer...

00:03:13.762 --> 00:03:16.959
I just have to wait
a little longer...

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:21.567
This is First Officer Yamamoto
of the destroyer Soyokaze!

00:03:21.837 --> 00:03:22.895
Ah, it's you.

00:03:23.072 --> 00:03:27.943
Sir, I apologize for jumping
the chain of command like this...

00:03:27.943 --> 00:03:31.344
...but there's something I
must bring to your attention...

00:03:31.647 --> 00:03:34.081
...about that battle
with the Raalgon!

00:03:34.984 --> 00:03:40.149
Sir, it wasn't a victory at all!
It was simple luck!

00:03:40.289 --> 00:03:42.484
You could even say
it was an accident!

00:03:43.259 --> 00:03:46.524
The fact that headquarters
summoned the captain...

00:03:46.862 --> 00:03:49.092
...must be because
they reviewed my report.

00:03:49.832 --> 00:03:53.268
They must be planning
to punish him!

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.801
You can't make a fool
of the military, Tylor!

00:04:05.581 --> 00:04:09.017
Captain Tylor of the Soyokaze,
reporting as ordered, sir.

00:04:09.418 --> 00:04:11.409
Wow, what a pretty flag!

00:04:11.987 --> 00:04:15.218
The UPSF has all
sorts of cool stuff!

00:04:15.591 --> 00:04:17.616
Can I get one of these
for the Soyokaze?

00:04:17.793 --> 00:04:18.953
Captain Tylor!

00:04:19.128 --> 00:04:19.617
Yes, sir?

00:04:19.995 --> 00:04:22.020
We've called you
here for one reason.

00:04:22.231 --> 00:04:25.962
The high command is very impressed
that you, with a single ship...

00:04:26.268 --> 00:04:28.964
...destroyed an entire Raalgon
reconnaissance fleet.

00:04:29.138 --> 00:04:30.400
So you're going
to give me something?!

00:04:32.975 --> 00:04:35.102
But you already
sent us a new nurse.

00:04:35.311 --> 00:04:37.646
Oh, no. She was assigned
to the Soyokaze...

00:04:37.646 --> 00:04:40.843
...to take care of the
health of the entire crew.

00:04:41.383 --> 00:04:45.376
What we're giving you today is
especially for you, Captain Tylor.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.290
The United Planets Order
of Merit, second class.

00:04:50.359 --> 00:04:52.327
Take it with
our compliments.

00:04:54.296 --> 00:04:56.821
So, what am I supposed
to do with this thing?

00:04:58.867 --> 00:04:59.959
Oh, well.

00:05:01.303 --> 00:05:04.295
When the timer activates the
chip we planted in Tylor's medal...

00:05:04.373 --> 00:05:09.242
...it'll access the
Soyokaze's radio transmitter...

00:05:09.311 --> 00:05:11.745
...and make the ship look
like a huge fleet on radar.

00:05:11.947 --> 00:05:13.282
A fleet that large...

00:05:13.282 --> 00:05:17.616
...will draw a Raalgon
fleet like ants to honey.

00:05:18.387 --> 00:05:20.184
That's when we'll fire...

00:05:20.256 --> 00:05:22.224
...the super interplanetary
ballistic missile Ohka at them.

00:05:24.927 --> 00:05:26.690
The Raalgon fleet
will be destroyed.

00:05:26.829 --> 00:05:30.321
Of course, the Soyokaze will be
honorably blasted to star dust.

00:05:30.466 --> 00:05:32.525
When is it set to activate?

00:05:32.768 --> 00:05:34.133
15:00 hours.

00:05:34.403 --> 00:05:35.768
I can't wait.

00:05:36.338 --> 00:05:39.603
But why are you trying to
destroy one of our own ships?

00:05:40.943 --> 00:05:45.778
Never mind. I won't refuse a
request from you, Admiral.

00:05:46.115 --> 00:05:50.211
Of course, I may ask for
a favor from you one day.

00:05:50.452 --> 00:05:53.751
"The enemy lies within"
rings ever more true.

00:06:03.365 --> 00:06:07.529
Go to point 1309 via point 874?

00:06:07.736 --> 00:06:12.264
Those are strange orders.
Why send one ship out on that route?

00:06:12.441 --> 00:06:13.738
What's our mission objective?

00:06:13.876 --> 00:06:16.367
Dunno. They didn't
tell me anything.

00:06:16.779 --> 00:06:21.512
I don't believe it!
They didn't punish him at all?!

00:06:21.583 --> 00:06:23.642
I don't understand!
I just don't understand!

00:06:23.986 --> 00:06:28.286
What did the commanders
talk to him about?

00:06:36.165 --> 00:06:39.032
You little... Do you know
who you're talking to?!

00:06:39.101 --> 00:06:41.069
Admiral Donan, commander of...

00:06:41.136 --> 00:06:44.401
...the 23rd galactic
frontier division, of course.

00:06:44.473 --> 00:06:48.773
Then watch your damn mouth!
I don't need any help from you!

00:06:48.844 --> 00:06:50.641
Well, then, I beg your pardon.

00:06:55.718 --> 00:06:56.776
Donan...

00:06:57.486 --> 00:07:02.150
I pity the Earthers for having
to fight such a disgusting man.

00:07:03.459 --> 00:07:05.791
All ships! Begin
wide-area sensor sweeps!

00:07:05.861 --> 00:07:09.422
We're going to wipe out
the UPSF once and for all!

00:07:23.812 --> 00:07:28.181
At last, a battle...
I can finally cut loose.

00:07:28.884 --> 00:07:30.146
But it's funny...

00:07:30.219 --> 00:07:31.447
What's funny?

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:34.318
We don't get orders till
we get to the mission area.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:36.822
And we have to fly to the
battle zone all on our own.

00:07:36.892 --> 00:07:39.258
You're over thinking this.
That's not like you.

00:07:39.561 --> 00:07:41.825
All we gotta do is
carry out our mission.

00:07:41.897 --> 00:07:42.989
That's not what I mean!

00:07:43.232 --> 00:07:44.324
Then what?

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:49.166
It's hard to explain, but...
It just seems too quiet.

00:07:49.405 --> 00:07:50.565
Too quiet?

00:07:50.906 --> 00:07:51.838
Yeah.

00:07:52.741 --> 00:07:53.935
Space Cards

00:07:56.512 --> 00:07:57.809
Space Cards.

00:07:57.913 --> 00:07:59.312
I can see that!

00:07:59.548 --> 00:08:02.244
Since we're all bored,
I figured we could play.

00:08:02.584 --> 00:08:04.575
While we're on duty?!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:05.648
I don't mind.

00:08:06.288 --> 00:08:10.190
Captain! Need I remind you
that a man in your position...

00:08:10.259 --> 00:08:13.751
...has to set a good
example to his men?!

00:08:14.263 --> 00:08:17.198
Don't forget that even though
we're just on a solo flight...

00:08:17.266 --> 00:08:20.531
...for an unexplained reason, the
crew thinks it's a secret mission.

00:08:20.602 --> 00:08:24.902
So, I figured playing cards
would calm everyone down.

00:08:25.441 --> 00:08:26.275
Can't do it?

00:08:26.275 --> 00:08:27.207
No, you can't!

00:08:27.576 --> 00:08:32.343
He really is just an idiot.
What's wrong with the military?!

00:08:32.548 --> 00:08:35.517
I would gladly sacrifice
myself for the Force...

00:08:35.584 --> 00:08:38.883
...but I cannot work
under this fool!

00:08:38.987 --> 00:08:40.352
Mr. Yamamoto?

00:08:40.489 --> 00:08:41.547
This fool!

00:08:42.391 --> 00:08:44.450
Um, uh, this
foolishly quiet trip...

00:08:44.526 --> 00:08:47.461
...is just the thing to
allow our minds and bodies...

00:08:47.529 --> 00:08:49.429
...to rest up from
the daily grind!

00:08:49.565 --> 00:08:52.557
Exactly! And playing
Space Cards will help!

00:08:52.634 --> 00:08:53.566
Captain!

00:08:54.303 --> 00:08:56.203
I know, we can't do it.

00:08:56.972 --> 00:08:59.532
God, I wish the enemy would
show up and break the boredom!

00:08:59.608 --> 00:09:01.576
Sir, don't say that!
If a single destroyer...

00:09:01.643 --> 00:09:03.838
...were to encounter an
enemy fleet out here...

00:09:03.912 --> 00:09:06.176
Enemy fleet sighted 8.5
light seconds ahead!

00:09:06.648 --> 00:09:07.910
I'll put it on screen!

00:09:10.252 --> 00:09:12.379
All right! We found
some enemy ships!

00:09:12.654 --> 00:09:14.747
No, some enemy ships
have found us!

00:09:15.557 --> 00:09:17.457
Just one destroyer, huh?

00:09:18.994 --> 00:09:22.930
No matter. I'll pound
the hell out of them...

00:09:22.998 --> 00:09:25.091
...till they're nothing
but space dust!

00:09:26.335 --> 00:09:28.633
All ships, open fire!

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:39.470
Sir, give the order to fire!

00:09:40.015 --> 00:09:41.778
Ready, set... Run!

00:09:51.627 --> 00:09:53.390
Captain!
Give the order to fire!

00:09:56.965 --> 00:09:58.330
Captain!

00:10:06.942 --> 00:10:10.673
The barrier can't protect
us from fire this intense!

00:10:10.846 --> 00:10:11.904
Lieutenant Yamamoto!

00:10:13.882 --> 00:10:16.612
Now I'll show them how
a REAL captain acts!

00:10:17.386 --> 00:10:20.378
I'm assuming command!
Commence return fire!

00:10:22.357 --> 00:10:23.654
Seven photon torpedo bays,
destroyed!

00:10:23.725 --> 00:10:25.317
Six phaser banks, destroyed!

00:10:25.394 --> 00:10:27.828
All long-range laser cannons have
been destroyed! That is all.

00:10:29.398 --> 00:10:31.127
All ships, cease fire!

00:10:31.667 --> 00:10:35.603
Target the enemy vessel and link
fire control systems to the Baroume!

00:10:43.612 --> 00:10:46.672
All ships now targeting
enemy vessel, sir!

00:10:47.749 --> 00:10:50.274
I'll put them
out of their misery.

00:10:51.053 --> 00:10:53.021
Ohka overhaul
and repairs completed.

00:10:53.088 --> 00:10:55.022
All blocks read in the green!

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.523
Returning to base.

00:10:56.592 --> 00:10:59.561
Roger. Now docking
space launches.

00:11:15.777 --> 00:11:17.846
Soon now, Admiral...

00:11:17.846 --> 00:11:18.744
Shut up!

00:11:18.981 --> 00:11:22.217
Admiral! Enemy fleet engaging
the Soyokaze at point 1309...

00:11:22.217 --> 00:11:23.650
Just be quiet!

00:11:25.787 --> 00:11:28.551
All ships will have
firing solutions shortly.

00:11:35.464 --> 00:11:37.898
Lemme go!
Don't you understand?!

00:11:37.966 --> 00:11:41.333
You idiot! If you launch now,
they'll pick you off!

00:11:41.403 --> 00:11:44.172
If I'm gonna die, let it be
with my hands on the controls!

00:11:44.172 --> 00:11:45.969
You think your death
will mean something?!

00:11:46.041 --> 00:11:47.633
Of course it'll mean something!

00:11:47.909 --> 00:11:50.605
How can you be a soldier
and not understand that?!

00:11:50.679 --> 00:11:51.805
They're right!

00:11:53.048 --> 00:11:54.913
We're going out in the dropship!

00:11:55.817 --> 00:11:57.717
I dunno what our mission is...

00:11:57.786 --> 00:12:01.051
...but if we're gonna die,
we're gonna die in style!

00:12:01.456 --> 00:12:02.388
Guys...

00:12:02.724 --> 00:12:04.988
That's how men should act!

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.651
Well, they aren't born
with them just for show.

00:12:07.829 --> 00:12:09.057
Right!

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.191
Farewell, Tylor.

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:50.797
Wha?! Where'd that
fleet come from?!

00:12:50.972 --> 00:12:54.840
Damn, this destroyer
must be out here as bait!

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:58.702
All ships, target enemy fleet and
initiate emergency subspace jump!

00:13:05.821 --> 00:13:08.483
Long live youth!
Long live humanity!

00:13:08.724 --> 00:13:11.022
Long live the United
Planets Space Force!

00:13:13.195 --> 00:13:15.288
Huh? What are you
doing, Mr. Yamamoto?

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:19.724
The... The enemy?!

00:13:19.901 --> 00:13:21.630
Well...

00:13:21.903 --> 00:13:24.167
They all just warped out
of here for some reason.

00:13:24.439 --> 00:13:26.634
They warped?!
What do you mean?!

00:13:26.908 --> 00:13:30.309
Well, they must have
run away, Mr. Yamamoto.

00:13:30.412 --> 00:13:32.403
Run away?! Impossible!

00:13:33.048 --> 00:13:34.948
Say, isn't it time to eat?

00:13:35.884 --> 00:13:37.681
You idiot!

00:13:38.487 --> 00:13:40.853
Radio wave field
surrounding our fleet!

00:13:40.922 --> 00:13:43.083
Enemy raid! Enemy raid!

00:13:43.258 --> 00:13:44.520
What's going on?!

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.888
But we saw Tylor take the medal!

00:13:59.508 --> 00:14:00.975
Kill them all!

00:14:21.897 --> 00:14:23.364
This is incredible!

00:15:00.969 --> 00:15:04.598
I've always thought of battlefields
as tasteless, barren places...

00:15:04.673 --> 00:15:06.766
...but I've never
seen one this beautiful.

00:15:07.142 --> 00:15:08.871
Yeah. Me, neither.

00:15:09.644 --> 00:15:13.375
If I'd died before,
I never could have seen this.

00:15:14.049 --> 00:15:15.744
It's just like
you said, Mr. Yamamoto.

00:15:16.651 --> 00:15:19.620
This foolishly quiet
trip is just the thing...

00:15:19.688 --> 00:15:23.317
...to allow our minds and bodies
to rest up from the daily grind.

00:15:23.692 --> 00:15:26.320
Did... Did I say that?

00:15:26.628 --> 00:15:27.720
Now I understand!

00:15:28.363 --> 00:15:30.797
Why headquarters really
ordered us out here.

00:15:30.966 --> 00:15:34.231
Admiral Mifune
wanted to reward us...

00:15:34.302 --> 00:15:36.770
...so he's given us this
beautiful sight as a present.

00:15:38.306 --> 00:15:41.543
Mr. Yamamoto, fighting in
a beautiful place like this...

00:15:41.543 --> 00:15:42.737
...would just be a waste.

00:15:46.681 --> 00:15:47.773
Don't you agree?

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:49.382
Yes, sir.

00:16:29.791 --> 00:16:33.557
All ships! Defend the Ho-Oh,
no matter what the cost!

00:16:33.762 --> 00:16:36.356
Kill them! Kill them all!

00:16:37.032 --> 00:16:39.364
Admiral Donan! I'm reading
a huge energy source...

00:16:39.434 --> 00:16:41.095
...to the rear of the enemy fleet!

00:16:43.638 --> 00:16:46.971
Good!
We'll blow it to atoms!

00:16:47.442 --> 00:16:51.674
An officer of Donan's rank
picks a fight with an enemy...

00:16:51.746 --> 00:16:53.941
...before investigating
who they are?

00:16:54.015 --> 00:16:56.813
His tactical skill is even
worse than his looks!

00:16:58.386 --> 00:17:01.150
After you invited us
all here, Doctor...

00:17:01.456 --> 00:17:03.549
...I wish Mr. Yamamoto
and the others had come.

00:17:03.792 --> 00:17:06.226
Only people who like
to drink should drink.

00:17:06.328 --> 00:17:09.126
When you get drunk,
it should be by your own choice.

00:17:09.597 --> 00:17:12.300
This stuff is best
with good scenery.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:14.700
Almost as good when you're
drinking under the stars.

00:17:14.769 --> 00:17:15.804
Here you go.

00:17:15.804 --> 00:17:20.264
Sorry to bother you with
such trivial work, Harumi.

00:17:20.475 --> 00:17:22.272
This is part of my duties, too.

00:17:22.377 --> 00:17:23.901
Want some, Harumi?

00:17:24.045 --> 00:17:25.672
No, thank you.

00:17:25.981 --> 00:17:26.572
Okay.

00:17:28.083 --> 00:17:30.347
Hm, you're a
real drinker, Captain.

00:17:30.652 --> 00:17:33.416
Hey, I'm twenty years old.

00:17:33.788 --> 00:17:35.722
I can buy alcohol
and cigarettes, too.

00:17:35.824 --> 00:17:36.552
Here you go.

00:17:36.791 --> 00:17:37.553
Thank you.

00:17:38.927 --> 00:17:42.330
A beautiful woman,
nice scenery, and a good drink.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:45.766
What more do I need?
Man, I'm glad I joined the Force!

00:17:46.034 --> 00:17:50.971
I wonder if the stars are laughing
at our war with the Raalgon?

00:17:51.673 --> 00:17:55.404
Why did you join up, Captain?

00:17:55.577 --> 00:17:56.737
Because I wanted an easy life.

00:17:57.012 --> 00:17:58.445
You wanted an easy life?

00:17:59.114 --> 00:18:00.138
That's just like you, Captain!

00:18:00.382 --> 00:18:02.373
Why'd you become a surgeon, Doc?

00:18:02.484 --> 00:18:05.783
Well, 'cuz I figured it was
better than being a patient.

00:18:06.021 --> 00:18:07.155
Can't argue with that!

00:18:07.155 --> 00:18:10.852
Compared to the universe,
we and the Raalgon are nothing.

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:16.794
Now targeting. Fire control
transferred to the Baroume!

00:18:17.732 --> 00:18:21.793
Admiral! The enemy fleet
is targeting the Ohka!

00:18:21.936 --> 00:18:23.371
They're what?!

00:18:23.371 --> 00:18:26.274
What the hell are the
idiots in our fleet doing?!

00:18:26.274 --> 00:18:30.142
If they can't defend one carrier and
allow the Ohka, the product of...

00:18:30.211 --> 00:18:34.549
...all our military science and
technology to be destroyed...

00:18:34.549 --> 00:18:40.488
...then the UPSF... No, I'LL be
the laughingstock of the universe!

00:18:40.688 --> 00:18:41.950
Protect that ship,
no matter what!

00:18:42.157 --> 00:18:46.423
Aye, sir! I'll broadcast your
exact words, Admiral!

00:18:47.328 --> 00:18:48.522
Targeting complete!

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:26.897
ALL SHIPS, PULL BACK!!!

00:19:34.943 --> 00:19:37.912
Why do people fight, Captain?

00:19:42.617 --> 00:19:46.314
Good grief... Either he's a fool
or an out and out genius.

00:19:47.155 --> 00:19:50.124
Genius? Tylor, a genius?

00:19:56.598 --> 00:19:58.088
Damn it!

00:20:00.635 --> 00:20:02.193
Bring me more!

00:20:03.872 --> 00:20:07.740
Admiral, I had the pleasure
of seeing you fight.

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:10.578
I'm on course to
rendezvous with you, sir.

00:20:10.745 --> 00:20:12.178
I don't need you to!

00:20:12.247 --> 00:20:13.111
As you wish.

00:20:20.655 --> 00:20:25.615
Man, it's a good thing you
drifted into our route, isn't it?

00:20:25.994 --> 00:20:29.361
Otherwise the Hizen might have
floated to the end of the universe.

00:20:30.965 --> 00:20:33.525
You know, pushing yourself
can be bad for your health.

00:20:33.968 --> 00:20:36.937
You have to think about
that at your age, sir.

00:20:38.673 --> 00:20:41.142
Uh, very impressive,
Captain Tylor!

00:20:41.142 --> 00:20:44.634
You really deserved that
special medal we gave you.

00:20:45.213 --> 00:20:47.113
Right, Admiral Mifune?

00:20:49.684 --> 00:20:53.586
Medal?! You gave
the captain a medal?!

00:20:53.721 --> 00:20:55.621
Oh? Didn't I tell you?

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:58.051
You're saying
it's actually true?!

00:21:01.029 --> 00:21:03.259
It can't be!
It can't be! It can't be!

00:21:12.307 --> 00:21:13.171
Huh?

00:21:13.708 --> 00:21:15.198
Must've lost it somewhere!

00:21:18.713 --> 00:21:20.415
I'm going to kill myself!

00:21:20.415 --> 00:21:21.712
Admiral Mifune!

00:21:21.883 --> 00:21:23.316
Sir, calm down!

00:21:23.384 --> 00:21:24.886
Let me go! Let me go!

00:21:24.886 --> 00:21:27.946
Don't do this over one medal!

00:21:28.122 --> 00:21:29.987
Shut up! I'm killing myself!

00:21:30.124 --> 00:21:31.192
Then can I help?

00:21:31.192 --> 00:21:32.318
What did you say?!

00:21:33.361 --> 00:21:35.563
And it was so pretty, too...
Admiral! You're the pride...

00:21:35.563 --> 00:21:35.730
And it was so pretty, too...
...of the UPSF! Don't be foolish!

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:37.332
...of the UPSF! Don't be foolish!

00:21:37.332 --> 00:21:38.066
Oh, well!
...of the UPSF! Don't be foolish!

00:21:38.066 --> 00:21:38.366
Oh, well!
I'm going to kill myself!

00:21:38.366 --> 00:21:41.096
I'm going to kill myself!

00:21:44.405 --> 00:21:47.306
Get someone up to block A-3!

00:22:12.467 --> 00:22:13.434
The Irresponsible Captain Tylor
Next Episode

00:22:14.802 --> 00:22:16.838
When cleaning's your specialty,
you're the cleaning officer.

00:22:16.838 --> 00:22:18.539
A giant cleanup at the
wrong time of the year.

00:22:18.539 --> 00:22:20.564
It takes many things
to make the Soyokaze.

00:22:20.675 --> 00:22:22.540
Will it all add
up to good fortune?

00:22:22.677 --> 00:22:25.237
Next time, "A Gentleman's
Word is His Bond."

